#
# Tepna — refill the hybrid-search index from doc-search's vector cache, so the index FOLLOWS the cache.
#
# WHY A SECOND UNIT. The server persists its documents, but it has no idea when the cache changes.
# `bge-reindex.timer` re-embeds new and edited files hourly; until this runs, `--hybrid` answers from a
# stale index while the default path answers from the fresh cache — the two lanes disagreeing is worse
# than either being behind, because a reader cannot tell which they got.
#
# 🔴 ORDERED AFTER THE RE-EMBED, NOT MERELY SCHEDULED NEAR IT. `After=bge-reindex.service` plus the
# timer's offset: the loader reads the cache, so running it DURING a re-embed would index a cache that is
# half-written — a file's vectors present, its neighbours' not. The loader's own validity rule (the body
# hash AND the chunk count must match) refuses such a file rather than pairing a stale vector with fresh
# text, so the failure mode is a SKIP, not corruption; but a skip means that file silently drops out of
# the index until the next tick. Ordering turns a silent gap into a non-event.
#
# IDEMPOTENT BY CONSTRUCTION, which is what makes an hourly tick safe. Every document's `_id` is
# `<path>#<chunk index>`, so a reload overwrites itself; it is also how this unit doubles as its own
# recovery step — a half-finished run is fixed by the next one, with no state to reconcile.
#
# 🔴 IT FAILS ON A LOAD OF ZERO, and that is deliberate. `xerj-load.mjs` exits non-zero when it loaded no
# document, because "nothing to do" and "the cache, the corpus or the staleness rule stopped matching"
# produce the same silence otherwise. A timer that reports success over an empty load is how a search
# index quietly empties.
#
# A MISSING TOOL OR SERVER IS NOT A GREEN RUN. If the loader is absent (not on main yet) the run exits 0
# with a line saying so and writes nothing — the previous state keeps its own timestamps and reads as
# stale rather than as fresh. If the server is down the loader's own refusal surfaces.
[Unit]
Description=Tepna — refill the hybrid-search index from the doc-search vector cache
Documentation=https://github.com/Plantucha/Tepna/blob/main/tools/xerj-load.mjs
After=bge-reindex.service tepna-hybrid-index.service
Wants=tepna-hybrid-index.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/Tepna
Nice=15
IOSchedulingClass=idle
# The loader refuses a non-loopback --url outright, so no address is passed: the default is 127.0.0.1
# and overriding it here would be the one place a reviewer would not look for a network change.
ExecStart=/bin/sh -c '[ -f tools/xerj-load.mjs ] || { echo "xerj-load.mjs not on origin/main yet — nothing to run, index left as it was"; exit 0; }; node tools/xerj-load.mjs --json'
